"use strict";(self.webpackChunkstapledons_voyage_site=self.webpackChunkstapledons_voyage_site||[]).push([[4820],{8406(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"/2026/10/10/bridge-consoles-and-stellar-radii","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/10/bridge-consoles-and-stellar-radii","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-10-bridge-consoles-and-stellar-radii.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-10-bridge-consoles-and-stellar-radii.mdx","title":"The bridge is where you decide","description":"Clocks, speed and distance stay visible as you travel. Course plotting and journey commitments now live at the bridge consoles, while M opens a read-only star chart wherever you are.","date":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"The bridge is where you decide","date":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","journey"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Visit Sgr A*: v0.4.0-dev.23 and dev.24","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/09/black-hole-v0-4-0-dev-23"}},"content":"Clocks, speed and distance stay visible as you travel. Course plotting and journey commitments now live at the bridge consoles, while **M** opens a read-only star chart wherever you are.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![The navigation station, with the two clocks above the helm](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/site/1ad5b1d2fb59ef335b0726753876f617796227095adeaee0e40f3a15f4832cb0.png)\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **A quieter HUD.** Both clocks share the status strip with your speed, phase and distance. Transit, arrival and gravity cards appear when relevant and keep the central outlook clear. [PR #193](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/193).\\n- **Decisions at the consoles.** Plot and commit at the navigation station, start a guided voyage at the Voyage console, and read the physics codex at the Archive terminal. Walk there, click to walk, or use the keyboard\'s Walk-to list; a press-twice confirmation option accompanies the hold. [PR #195](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/195).\\n- **A chart you can open anywhere.** M shows the neighbourhood without planning, committing or pausing. Tour pause and skip controls stay instant; the decisions have no countdown. [PR #195](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/195).\\n- **Sizes for more stars.** Catalogue stars without measured radii now get estimates from their brightness, distance and temperature, labelled as inferred. Barnard\'s Star becomes a visible disc at its stop. Body cards also explain synchronous orbits, including when no such orbit is possible. [PR #194](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/194).\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nThe first-journey slice still needs its complete console-based playthrough audit and remaining visual acceptance gates. Real interstellar clouds and individual dust impacts are being built on a separate branch and still await validation and render review.\\n\\nThis is a progress update between releases. [See the new captures in the gallery](/gallery)."},{"id":"/2026/10/09/black-hole-v0-4-0-dev-23","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/09/black-hole-v0-4-0-dev-23","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-09-black-hole-v0-4-0-dev-23.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-09-black-hole-v0-4-0-dev-23.mdx","title":"Visit Sgr A*: v0.4.0-dev.23 and dev.24","description":"The black-hole milestone is done: you can fly to the supermassive black hole at the centre of the Galaxy, hover above it and orbit it, with general relativity in the physics and in the picture.","date":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Sky","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/sky","description":"The relativistic sky and the star catalogues."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Visit Sgr A*: v0.4.0-dev.23 and dev.24","date":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","sky"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.24-lens-fix","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.24-lens-fix"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"The bridge is where you decide","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/10/bridge-consoles-and-stellar-radii"},"nextItem":{"title":"Stops that show scale, and the way home: v0.4.0-dev.25","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/09/free-navigation-v0-4-0-dev-25"}},"content":"The black-hole milestone is done: you can fly to the supermassive black hole at the centre of the Galaxy, hover above it and orbit it, with general relativity in the physics and in the picture.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![Sgr A* from the bridge at 10 Schwarzschild radii](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/refs/m3_bh_ship/bh_bridge_r10_hover.png)\\n\\n## Sgr A* aboard the ship\\n\\nChoose \\"Sgr A* (black hole)\\" in navigation. The ship approaches from 1.3 light years, then hovers at 10, 5 and 3 Schwarzschild radii and orbits at 3. The HUD reads the simulation:\\n\\n- **Clocks.** At 10 r_s, 1 ship-hour is 1.054 home hours; in orbit at 3 r_s it is 1.41. The time you spend near the hole really accumulates on both clocks.\\n- **Light.** It shows the shadow\'s size and the blueshift of incoming light.\\n- **Forces.** It shows the tide across the bubble, and the hover thrust, which the crew never feels.\\n\\n## Built package-first\\n\\n- **The maths.** `sunholo/relativity` 0.10.0 adds a geodesic integrator, cross-checked against the exact solution to 3e-13.\\n- **The lens tables.** They are generated on the AILANG VM and pinned.\\n- **The shader.** A GPU shader mirrors the CPU reference pixel for pixel.\\n- **The checks.** The shadow matches Synge\'s formula to within 0.01 px at 10, 5 and 3 r_s, and a star directly behind the hole makes an Einstein ring at the predicted angle. R1\'s black-hole requirements are met.\\n\\n## Also\\n\\n- **A light-speed loading screen.** Picking a menu option accelerates the real sky to 0.99999c, where it collapses into a point, then a white-out into the ship. Loading itself is 3 to 4 times faster.\\n- **A Main menu button** on the galaxy map.\\n- **dev.24 fixes dev.23.** The exported app was missing the lens tables, so the hole was invisible. Publishing now checks them inside the exported app.\\n\\n**Releases:** [v0.4.0-dev.23-black-hole](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.23-black-hole), [v0.4.0-dev.24-lens-fix](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.24-lens-fix) \xb7 [Gallery](/gallery)."},{"id":"/2026/10/09/free-navigation-v0-4-0-dev-25","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/09/free-navigation-v0-4-0-dev-25","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-09-free-navigation-v0-4-0-dev-25.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-09-free-navigation-v0-4-0-dev-25.mdx","title":"Stops that show scale, and the way home: v0.4.0-dev.25","description":"Wherever you stop, the size of what you see now tells you how big it really is. Sol is back on the map, and you can hop between the bodies of a system yourself.","date":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Stops that show scale, and the way home: v0.4.0-dev.25","date":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.25-free-nav","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.25-free-nav"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Visit Sgr A*: v0.4.0-dev.23 and dev.24","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/09/black-hole-v0-4-0-dev-23"},"nextItem":{"title":"Back to 60 fps, and inspect what you orbit: v0.4.0-dev.21","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/08/perf-inspect-v0-4-0-dev-21"}},"content":"Wherever you stop, the size of what you see now tells you how big it really is. Sol is back on the map, and you can hop between the bodies of a system yourself.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![Saturn at its new stop, rings sweeping past](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/refs/dev25/stop_7_saturn_sky_auto.png)\\n\\n## Stops that show relative size\\n\\nEvery stop used to show a planet at the same 60\xb0, and every star from 1,000 AU as a point. Now apparent size grows with true size, on smooth curves that never put the ship inside anything:\\n\\n- **Planets and moons.** The Moon is 16\xb0, Earth 30\xb0 and Jupiter 84\xb0; Saturn\'s stop clears its main rings.\\n- **Stars, in free navigation.** TRAPPIST-1 is 3.5\xb0, \u03b1 Centauri A 11\xb0 and Aldebaran 61\xb0. Stars with a measured radius get the rule now, and every other star will follow once the package can infer sizes from catalogue data.\\n\\n## Home, and in-system\\n\\n- **Sol.** It is clickable on the map, and **Return to Sol** arrives beside Earth.\\n- **In this system.** A list offers every planet, moon and star of the system you are in, and refuses legs that are physically impossible (through Jupiter), saying why.\\n- **When stopped.** The HUD shows where you are, where you came from and how far from Earth.\\n- **The I key.** It now works on the star you have stopped at.\\n- **Auto view.** It is the default, and the game remembers your choice.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.4.0-dev.25-free-nav](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.25-free-nav) \xb7 [Gallery](/gallery)."},{"id":"/2026/10/08/perf-inspect-v0-4-0-dev-21","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/08/perf-inspect-v0-4-0-dev-21","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-08-perf-inspect-v0-4-0-dev-21.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-08-perf-inspect-v0-4-0-dev-21.mdx","title":"Back to 60 fps, and inspect what you orbit: v0.4.0-dev.21","description":"dev.20\'s full sky made the laptop stutter at Aldebaran. One line was scanning all 335,189 stars every frame. Fixed, measured on the MacBook Air, and the I key now shows the bodies around you.","date":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Sky","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/sky","description":"The relativistic sky and the star catalogues."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Back to 60 fps, and inspect what you orbit: v0.4.0-dev.21","date":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","sky"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.21-perf-inspect","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.21-perf-inspect"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Stops that show scale, and the way home: v0.4.0-dev.25","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/09/free-navigation-v0-4-0-dev-25"},"nextItem":{"title":"A title screen, and a first look at a black hole: v0.4.0-dev.22","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/08/title-screen-v0-4-0-dev-22"}},"content":"dev.20\'s full sky made the laptop stutter at Aldebaran. One line was scanning all 335,189 stars every frame. Fixed, measured on the MacBook Air, and the I key now shows the bodies around you.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![Holding I at TRAPPIST-1](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/refs/dev22/inspect_trappist-1_held.png)\\n\\n## The lag\\n\\nA performance audit on the M2 Air at the Aldebaran stop showed 53 fps, and 30 fps in the overview. Switching suspects off one at a time on the Studio cleared the new ship lighting and pointed at the 100 pc sky. Timing the per-frame calls found it: a check that ran every frame compared each nearby star against all 335,189 star identities, one by one, before deciding nothing had changed. That took 13.7 ms of a 16.7 ms frame. With a hash lookup it takes 0.01 ms.\\n\\nOn the Air, the same stop now runs at 60 fps at the median in every view, the overview included, with no frame over 25 ms. A regression test fails if this cost ever grows with the number of stars again.\\n\\n## Hold I\\n\\nHolding I used to ring only background stars. Now it also rings the Sun, planets, moons, finite stars and exoplanets, at the size they are drawn, aberration included. Click one for its card: distance, size and apparent size, temperature, how long ago its light left, and its data source.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.4.0-dev.21-perf-inspect](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.21-perf-inspect) \xb7 [Gallery](/gallery) \xb7 PRs #155, #156."},{"id":"/2026/10/08/title-screen-v0-4-0-dev-22","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/08/title-screen-v0-4-0-dev-22","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-08-title-screen-v0-4-0-dev-22.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-08-title-screen-v0-4-0-dev-22.mdx","title":"A title screen, and a first look at a black hole: v0.4.0-dev.22","description":"The game now opens on a menu. Meanwhile the black-hole milestone is two-thirds built: the first renders of Sgr A*\'s lensed sky are in, checked against general relativity to a fraction of a pixel.","date":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Sky","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/sky","description":"The relativistic sky and the star catalogues."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"A title screen, and a first look at a black hole: v0.4.0-dev.22","date":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","sky"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.22-title-screen","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.22-title-screen"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Back to 60 fps, and inspect what you orbit: v0.4.0-dev.21","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/08/perf-inspect-v0-4-0-dev-21"},"nextItem":{"title":"Stars with real size: v0.4.0-dev.19","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/07/finite-stars-v0-4-0-dev-19"}},"content":"The game now opens on a menu. Meanwhile the black-hole milestone is two-thirds built: the first renders of Sgr A*\'s lensed sky are in, checked against general relativity to a fraction of a pixel.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![The title screen](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/refs/dev22/title.png)\\n\\n## The title screen\\n\\nA double-click opens a menu over the real Milky Way: **Board the ship**, the **Guided voyage**, the **Galaxy map**, **Settings** (Realistic or Auto view, text-only AI) and **Credits**, read from the repository\'s own citations. Esc in the ship returns to it.\\n\\n## Black holes (in progress)\\n\\n![Sgr A* at 5 Schwarzschild radii](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/refs/m3_bh/mw_r5_toward_hover.png)\\n\\nM3 brings general relativity:\\n\\n- **The maths is in the package first.** `sunholo/relativity` 0.10.0 adds a geodesic integrator, cross-checked against the exact solution to 3e-13.\\n- **The sim reports what you would feel.** Clock rates, tides across the bubble, and the thrust to hover, all at Sgr A*.\\n- **A GPU shader bends the sky.** It reads lens tables generated on the AILANG VM.\\n\\nThe shadow matches Synge\'s formula to within 0.01 px at 10, 5 and 3 r_s. A star directly behind the hole becomes an Einstein ring at the predicted angle; just off-axis, it splits into two images.\\n\\nThe playable trip is next: hover at 10, 5 and 3 r_s, then orbit, from the bridge. The HUD reads the sim, so \\"1 ship-hour = 1.41 home hours\\" in orbit at 3 r_s.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.4.0-dev.22-title-screen](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.22-title-screen) \xb7 [Gallery](/gallery)."},{"id":"/2026/10/07/finite-stars-v0-4-0-dev-19","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/07/finite-stars-v0-4-0-dev-19","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-07-finite-stars-v0-4-0-dev-19.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-07-finite-stars-v0-4-0-dev-19.mdx","title":"Stars with real size: v0.4.0-dev.19","description":"Until now only the Sun and \u03b1 Centauri had a size; every other star you visited was a point seen from 1,000 AU away. Now each star in the voyage is a real disc with its measured radius and temperature, and you arrive where its size means something.","date":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Stars with real size: v0.4.0-dev.19","date":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.19-finite-stars","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.19-finite-stars"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"A title screen, and a first look at a black hole: v0.4.0-dev.22","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/08/title-screen-v0-4-0-dev-22"},"nextItem":{"title":"Real exoplanets, real starlight: v0.4.0-dev.20","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/07/trappist-planets-v0-4-0-dev-20"}},"content":"Until now only the Sun and \u03b1 Centauri had a size; every other star you visited was a point seen from 1,000 AU away. Now each star in the voyage is a real disc with its measured radius and temperature, and you arrive where its size means something.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![Aldebaran filling 40 degrees of sky](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/refs/finite_stars_v19/9_aldebaran_arrived.png)\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **Aldebaran** (45 solar radii, 3,927 K) and **TRAPPIST-1** (0.119 solar radii, 2,566 K) are finite stars with cited measurements, in place of catalogue points.\\n- **One stop rule.** Main-sequence stars stop in their habitable zone, where they look like the Sun from Earth: \u03b1 Cen A at 1.233 AU, about half a degree; TRAPPIST-1 at 0.0235 AU, a deep-orange disc 2.7\xb0 across beside where its planets orbit. Giants stop where they fill 40\xb0 of sky: Aldebaran from 0.615 AU.\\n- **The same rhythm everywhere.** Each star\'s final hop is 30 s accelerating, about a minute cruising, then the 25 s final approach, like the planets.\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nAldebaran is so bright at 40\xb0 that it reads white; dimmed, it is pale orange. Its approach is still relativistic, since it is already 4\xb0 across six AU out. Both are open questions. TRAPPIST-1\'s seven planets are next.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.4.0-dev.19-finite-stars](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.19-finite-stars) \xb7 [Gallery](/gallery) \xb7 Integration [PR #139](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/139)."},{"id":"/2026/10/07/trappist-planets-v0-4-0-dev-20","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/07/trappist-planets-v0-4-0-dev-20","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-07-trappist-planets-v0-4-0-dev-20.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-07-trappist-planets-v0-4-0-dev-20.mdx","title":"Real exoplanets, real starlight: v0.4.0-dev.20","description":"The voyage now reaches a real planetary system, the ship is lit by whichever star it is near, and the sky holds six times more stars, each in exactly one place.","date":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Real exoplanets, real starlight: v0.4.0-dev.20","date":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.20-trappist-planets","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.20-trappist-planets"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Stars with real size: v0.4.0-dev.19","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/07/finite-stars-v0-4-0-dev-19"},"nextItem":{"title":"Even legs and a gentle arrival: v0.4.0-dev.18","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/06/even-legs-v0-4-0-dev-18"}},"content":"The voyage now reaches a real planetary system, the ship is lit by whichever star it is near, and the sky holds six times more stars, each in exactly one place.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![TRAPPIST-1e from the habitable zone](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/refs/dev20/trappist-1e_tele12_auto.png)\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **TRAPPIST-1\'s seven planets.** At the habitable-zone stop, planets b\u2013h are where they really are when you arrive. Sizes and orbits come from Agol et al. 2021, positions from transit timings (Ducrot et al. 2020) corrected for 40.6 years of light travel. Planet e is 0.72\xb0 across, bigger than our Moon; c is a crescent and d half lit. Albedos and surfaces are assumed and labelled so.\\n- **The ship lit by the real star.** The bridge\'s key light comes from the Sun, or the star you are visiting, as seen through the bubble: its direction (aberration included), its colour (Doppler included) and a log-compressed brightness, labelled as not physical. Sun shadows sweep the deck as the ship turns; TRAPPIST-1 is a dim red glow; Aldebaran floods the deck with warm light. Deep space hands back to the ship\'s own lighting.\\n- **Star colours (D-49).** Auto view dims a star just enough to keep its hue and lifts its blackbody colour: Aldebaran golden orange, TRAPPIST-1 an ember. Realistic view is unchanged.\\n- **A giant\'s approach.** Aldebaran\'s final approach lasts 90 s, so the giant grows out of the starbow, blue-white at first from your own speed, turning golden as you stop.\\n- **One position per star.** Navigation and the sky now read a single truth table built in AILANG. Before, a map journey could arrive with the star drawn up to 8.7 ly away; now it\'s always ahead.\\n- **The full 100 pc sky.** 331,311 nearby stars from Gaia instead of about 50,000, for about 0.3 ms a frame.\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nYou can\'t fly to a TRAPPIST-1 planet yet, because its surface would have to be invented. The 100 pc sky\'s cost on a MacBook Air is an estimate (+1.3\u20131.8 ms) until measured.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.4.0-dev.20-trappist-planets](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.20-trappist-planets) \xb7 [Gallery](/gallery) \xb7 PRs #143, #146, #149."},{"id":"/2026/10/06/even-legs-v0-4-0-dev-18","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/06/even-legs-v0-4-0-dev-18","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-06-even-legs-v0-4-0-dev-18.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-06-even-legs-v0-4-0-dev-18.mdx","title":"Even legs and a gentle arrival: v0.4.0-dev.18","description":"Every Solar System leg now has the same rhythm, about 2\xbc minutes in real time: 30 seconds accelerating, about a minute cruising, then braking into a 25-second final approach. The longer legs simply go faster, above 0.999c to Jupiter and Saturn, so the planets now ease into view instead of appearing in the last few seconds.","date":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Even legs and a gentle arrival: v0.4.0-dev.18","date":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.18-even-legs","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.18-even-legs"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Real exoplanets, real starlight: v0.4.0-dev.20","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/07/trappist-planets-v0-4-0-dev-20"},"nextItem":{"title":"A real-time voyage to Aldebaran: v0.4.0-dev.17","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/06/real-time-voyage-v0-4-0-dev-17"}},"content":"Every Solar System leg now has the same rhythm, about 2\xbc minutes in real time: 30 seconds accelerating, about a minute cruising, then braking into a 25-second final approach. The longer legs simply go faster, above 0.999c to Jupiter and Saturn, so the planets now ease into view instead of appearing in the last few seconds.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![The HUD during the final approach to Jupiter](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/refs/even_legs_v18/hud_jupiter_final_approach.png)\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **Even legs.** The simulation solves each leg\'s thrust and cruise speed so the boost lasts 30 s and the cruise about 60 s: 0.07c for the short Callisto hop, 0.99943c (\u03b3 30) to Jupiter, 0.99963c (\u03b3 37) to Saturn. Sun \u2192 Jupiter takes about 2\xbc minutes instead of 6\xbd.\\n- **A gentle final approach.** A new trip profile brakes hard, then eases in for 25 s from where the planet is 4\xb0 across, so Jupiter grows smoothly instead of exploding in the last 8 s. It\'s built from the same exact constant-acceleration physics, in `sunholo/relativity` 0.9.0. The HUD says FINAL APPROACH.\\n- **Skip stage [K].** Jump to the next stage of the leg: accelerating \u2192 cruise \u2192 braking \u2192 final approach \u2192 arrival. It lands exactly on each stage, and the HUD counts how many you skipped.\\n- **Distances on the HUD:** to the destination, from the last stop, and from Earth, plus this leg\'s thrust.\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nAt the faster in-system speeds, the bubble wall\'s glow tints the forward view; how to present it is open. Stars beyond the Sun still appear as points: giving every visited star its real size (TRAPPIST-1, Aldebaran) is the next sprint.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.4.0-dev.18-even-legs](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.18-even-legs) \xb7 [Gallery](/gallery) \xb7 Integration [PR #134](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/134)."},{"id":"/2026/10/06/real-time-voyage-v0-4-0-dev-17","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/06/real-time-voyage-v0-4-0-dev-17","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-06-real-time-voyage-v0-4-0-dev-17.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-06-real-time-voyage-v0-4-0-dev-17.mdx","title":"A real-time voyage to Aldebaran: v0.4.0-dev.17","description":"The guided tour no longer fast-forwards. Every boost and every braking plays at one ship second per wall second, and special relativity, not a time-lapse, is what makes the trips short. Earth to Jupiter takes six minutes aboard while 39 pass on Earth. Then the voyage leaves the Sun behind: \u03b1 Centauri, TRAPPIST-1 and Aldebaran, 120 Earth years later.","date":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"A real-time voyage to Aldebaran: v0.4.0-dev.17","date":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.17-real-time-voyage","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.17-real-time-voyage"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Even legs and a gentle arrival: v0.4.0-dev.18","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/06/even-legs-v0-4-0-dev-18"},"nextItem":{"title":"Manual sky exposure and a one-AU arrival: v0.4.0-dev.14","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/05/stable-sky-and-one-au-arrival"}},"content":"The guided tour no longer fast-forwards. Every boost and every braking plays at one ship second per wall second, and special relativity, not a time-lapse, is what makes the trips short. Earth to Jupiter takes six minutes aboard while 39 pass on Earth. Then the voyage leaves the Sun behind: \u03b1 Centauri, TRAPPIST-1 and Aldebaran, 120 Earth years later.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![The cruise interlude on the way to Aldebaran: 0.999999c, \u03b3 707, everyone you knew is gone](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/refs/real_time_voyage_v17/7_aldebaran_card.png)\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **Real time, no compression.** A single drive (3,000,000 g, inertia-damped as the bubble\'s fiction allows) takes the Solar System legs to 0.99c. You watch the starbow form during each 27-second boost and unwind during braking. Both clocks are on the HUD, and they drift apart in front of you.\\n- **Further and faster.** \u03b1 Centauri at 0.999c, then TRAPPIST-1 at 0.9999c, then Aldebaran, 66.6 light-years away, at 0.999999c (\u03b3 707). The whole voyage is about 11 months aboard and 120 years at home.\\n- **Cruise interludes.** Interstellar cruises are long: 70, 216 and 38 days aboard. After the boost and ten seconds of cruise, the game hands over to an interlude. Today it is a card that states speed, \u03b3, both clocks, how old news from home is, and what the elapsed Earth time means. In the full game the interlude is where life aboard happens. Braking into each star plays in real time.\\n- **Stars where you arrive.** Two star catalogues disagreed about where some stars are, by up to thousands of AU, which only shows when you stop 1,000 AU away. Destinations now render exactly where the simulation flies.\\n- **A compact HUD:** where you\'re going, the phase, the speed (from the simulation\'s exact 1 \u2212 \u03b2), \u03b3, km/s and both clocks. The details are behind Tab.\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nTRAPPIST-1\'s seven planets are planned as a real stop; for now you arrive at the star. At the highest speeds the glowing bubble wall washes out the forward view; how to present that is an open design question. Ship lighting still doesn\'t follow the Sun.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.4.0-dev.17-real-time-voyage](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.17-real-time-voyage) \xb7 [Gallery](/gallery) \xb7 Integration [PR #130](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/130)."},{"id":"/2026/10/05/stable-sky-and-one-au-arrival","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/05/stable-sky-and-one-au-arrival","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-05-stable-sky-and-one-au-arrival.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-05-stable-sky-and-one-au-arrival.mdx","title":"Manual sky exposure and a one-AU arrival: v0.4.0-dev.14","description":"The painted ship and Solar departure tour share one perspective. This review build removes automatic sky dimming: exposure stays at your manually selected brightness while you move and look around. The tour finishes one AU from Alpha Centauri A.","date":"2026-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."},{"inline":false,"label":"Planets","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/planets","description":"Planets, moons and flybys (M5)."},{"inline":false,"label":"Art","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/art","description":"Concept and in-game art."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Manual sky exposure and a one-AU arrival: v0.4.0-dev.14","date":"2026-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey","planets","art"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.14-manual-sky","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.14-manual-sky"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"A real-time voyage to Aldebaran: v0.4.0-dev.17","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/06/real-time-voyage-v0-4-0-dev-17"},"nextItem":{"title":"Walkable bridge demo: v0.4.0-dev.1","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1"}},"content":"import DownloadCard from \'@site/src/components/DownloadCard\';\\n\\nThe painted ship and Solar departure tour share one perspective. This review build removes automatic sky dimming: exposure stays at your manually selected brightness while you move and look around. The tour finishes one AU from Alpha Centauri A.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n<DownloadCard compact />\\n\\n![Alpha Centauri A and its background stars at the actual one-AU stop, manual exposure](https://storage.googleapis.com/stapledons-voyage-assets/refs/manual_sky_v14/alpha_1au_pan_0.png)\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **One current painted ship:** seven major tiers, a bridge floor and captain shadow that meet the walking surface, faster movement, trackpad look and known-star inspection. [Integration PR](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/117).\\n- **Gradual approaches:** the guided tour uses physical 1 g acceleration with 90 seconds of braking playback. Earth, Jupiter and Saturn sit beside the bridge at their close stops. Ordinary navigation keeps its existing pacing. [Integration PR](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/117).\\n- **Manual sky exposure:** J cycles the brightness settings, also available under Tab. Bright planets and suns can wash out at a setting chosen for stars; camera pans and journeys no longer change exposure automatically. The physical light and SR calculations remain unchanged.\\n- **Smoother tour starts:** initialize the camera from the new session and ease departure time compression over three seconds. This corrects an initial camera jump and an abrupt first movement beside Earth.\\n- **Measured stars:** Alpha Centauri A/B use measured radii and temperatures; the final leg intercepts the moving primary at 1 AU. A\'s disc is about 0.65\xb0 wide there. [Integration PR](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/117).\\n- **Review evidence:** the gallery and geometry reference include fresh native captures and editable Blender masters. B keeps the full benchmark locally and attempts an authenticated upload of filtered aggregate measurements. [Integration PR](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/117).\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nShip lighting is still an internal lighting study; external sunlight, detailed moon surfaces and further Commons art remain in progress. Fresh M2 Air performance needs a laptop measurement. Tour stops are inertial clearance stops: gravity, thermal hazards and GR are not simulated. Stellar photospheres are uniform emitters.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.4.0-dev.14-manual-sky](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.14-manual-sky) \xb7 [Gallery](/gallery) \xb7 [Ship reference](/docs/ship-layer-reference)."},{"id":"/2026/10/03/walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1.mdx","title":"Walkable bridge demo: v0.4.0-dev.1","description":"A development build you can download: walk the captain around the bridge under the live","date":"2026-10-03T20:15:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."},{"inline":false,"label":"Art","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/art","description":"Concept and in-game art."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Walkable bridge demo: v0.4.0-dev.1","date":"2026-10-03T20:15","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey","art"],"release_tag":"v0.4.0-dev.1","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.1"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Manual sky exposure and a one-AU arrival: v0.4.0-dev.14","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/05/stable-sky-and-one-au-arrival"},"nextItem":{"title":"Concept art: the captain and the bridge","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge"}},"content":"import DownloadCard from \'@site/src/components/DownloadCard\';\\n\\nA development build you can download: walk the captain around the bridge under the live\\nrelativistic sky, open the galaxy map from the nav console, and fly a journey to \u03b1 Centauri A\\nthrough the bubble. macOS only, Apple Silicon.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n<DownloadCard compact />\\n\\n![The captain on the bridge at 0.99c, under the live relativistic sky](/img/news/bridge-demo-cruise.jpg)\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **The walkable bridge** (M4.2, [#102](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/102)): the bridge disc at the top of the spire,\\n  composited with the live sky through the same camera. The captain walks it (**WASD**, **E** to\\n  use) and ages with ship time.\\n- **Navigation from the bridge:** a nav console opens the galaxy map (**M**), built from the real\\n  catalogues: 5,685 stars within 25 pc, companions at their system\'s distance. Commit to \u03b1\\n  Centauri A and watch the boost, the 0.99c cruise, the brake and the arrival.\\n- **The relativistic sky** behind it all: 335k real stars, aberration and Doppler colour, the\\n  naked-eye exposure, and the forward glow of the cosmic background at extreme speed.\\n- **L** opens the log and **K** the codex.\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\n- The forward bubble-wall glow is off; it returns with the next simulation step.\\n- The standalone sky flight (`-- --voyage`) shows a mirrored sky in this build: fixed on main\\n  ([#107](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/107)), in the next build. The view\\n  from the bridge is correct.\\n- The bridge is v1 demo art; the final art is in progress ([concept art](/concept-art)).\\n- Pre-alpha and unsigned; see [Try it](/docs/try-it) for install notes.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.4.0-dev.1](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.4.0-dev.1) (macOS development build)"},{"id":"/2026/10/03/concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge.md","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge.md","title":"Concept art: the captain and the bridge","description":"The ship has faces now. The captain is picked, the crew have proposed portraits, and the bridge","date":"2026-10-03T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"Art","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/art","description":"Concept and in-game art."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Concept art: the captain and the bridge","date":"2026-10-03T18:00","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","art"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Walkable bridge demo: v0.4.0-dev.1","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Planets are coming","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/planets-are-coming"}},"content":"The ship has faces now. The captain is picked, the crew have proposed portraits, and the bridge\\nstands in the engine over the live sky.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n![The captain, the Longline Navigator, at 30, 50, 70 and 90](/img/concept/captain-sheet.jpg)\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **The captain, the Longline Navigator** ([#98](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/98)): picked from three silhouette\\n  proposals, and drawn front and back at 30, 50, 70 and 90, because the game spans a 100-year\\n  career.\\n- **Crew cast proposals**: one portrait per role, next to the Medic\'s accepted set.\\n- **Bridge v1** ([#97](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/97), demo art): the first real interior, a disc at the top of the\\n  spire inside the sphere ship. The sky behind the railings is not painted; it is the game\'s live\\n  sky, through the same camera, so at 0.99c it crowds forward and turns blue.\\n\\n![Bridge v1 in the engine at rest and at 0.99c](/img/concept/bridge-v1-parallax.jpg)\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nBridge v1 is demo art. A v2 quality study is done and the final art is being made. Everything is\\non the [concept art](/concept-art) page, labelled with its status."},{"id":"/2026/10/03/planets-are-coming","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/planets-are-coming","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-planets-are-coming.md","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-planets-are-coming.md","title":"Planets are coming","description":"A new milestone, M5, brings planets, moons and flybys inside a star system, with the same rule as","date":"2026-10-03T16:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"Planets","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/planets","description":"Planets, moons and flybys (M5)."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Planets are coming","date":"2026-10-03T16:00","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","planets"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Concept art: the captain and the bridge","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/concept-art-the-captain-and-the-bridge"},"nextItem":{"title":"The ship\'s AI foundation","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/the-ships-ai-foundation"}},"content":"A new milestone, M5, brings planets, moons and flybys inside a star system, with the same rule as\\nthe sky: real data, real physics.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s done\\n\\n- **The design and the sprint plan are approved** ([#84](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/84), [#86](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/86)).\\n- **A new AILANG package, [`sunholo/celestial`](https://github.com/sunholo-data/ailang-packages/tree/main/packages/celestial)\\n  0.1.0**, published with 93 tests: a Kepler solver, JPL planetary ephemerides for 3000 BC to\\n  3000 AD plus moons, IAU reference frames, light-time, gravity, reflectance, and planetary rings.\\n- **`sunholo/relativity` 0.6 and 0.7**: the bubble\'s forward glow, and the aberrated outline of a\\n  nearby sphere, which is what a planet looks like as you pass it near light speed.\\n\\n## What\'s planned\\n\\nStart held above Earth, pick a body on a system map (the Sun, 8 planets, 11 moons, 4 ring\\nsystems), choose to stop or fly by at 0.001c to 0.99c, commit, and ride the leg. The views will be\\nexact: light-time delay, aberration, and the Terrell rotation that makes a passing sphere look\\nturned. At \u03b1 Centauri, the known and candidate planets will show as points only, with a badge\\nsaying how sure the astronomy is. The first step, the Sol and \u03b1 Cen data and the game\'s package\\npins, has merged ([#99](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/99)).\\n\\nSee the [roadmap](/docs/roadmap)."},{"id":"/2026/10/03/the-ships-ai-foundation","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/the-ships-ai-foundation","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-the-ships-ai-foundation.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-the-ships-ai-foundation.mdx","title":"The ship\'s AI foundation","description":"The crew\'s optional AI layer runs end to end, so far on a deterministic test stub: lines with","date":"2026-10-03T15:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"AI","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/ai","description":"The optional crew AI layer."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"The ship\'s AI foundation","date":"2026-10-03T15:00","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","ai"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Planets are coming","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/planets-are-coming"},"nextItem":{"title":"A galaxy map from real catalogues","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues"}},"content":"import {ClipFigure} from \'@site/src/components/Clip\';\\n\\nThe crew\'s optional AI layer runs end to end, so far on a deterministic test stub: lines with\\nemotion markers, portraits that change with them, a voice, and a hard cost ceiling.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **Emotion markers** (AI.1\u2013AI.3): a line carries markers like `{loving}`, validated before the\\n  game uses it.\\n- **A service the game never waits on** (AI.4\u2013AI.7): provider routing, a cache, a supervised\\n  background process, and key hygiene: a key never appears on a command line.\\n- **The Medic\'s accepted portraits**, pinned and content-addressed (AI.8).\\n- **Opt-in and capped** (AI.9): live AI stays off until the player adds a key *and* ticks the box.\\n  A ceiling the player sets (US$0.50 by default) stops spending, and automated runs can never go\\n  live.\\n- **The conversation scene** (AI.10a, [#91](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/91)): the portrait cross-fades as each emotion\\n  marker arrives, the subtitles build segment by segment, and the voice plays.\\n\\n<ClipFigure name=\\"medic\\" sound caption=\\"The Medic scene on the stub. Placeholder voice: the stub\'s test tones, not a performance.\\" />\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nNo live model has been called. The first live run (AI.10b) is attended: one real line and a few\\nvoice auditions under a US$1 ceiling. The voice in the clip is a placeholder."},{"id":"/2026/10/03/a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues.md","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues.md","title":"A galaxy map from real catalogues","description":"The galaxy map now draws from the same star catalogues as the sky, and stars that belong together","date":"2026-10-03T12:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"Sky","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/sky","description":"The relativistic sky and the star catalogues."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"A galaxy map from real catalogues","date":"2026-10-03T12:00","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","sky","journey"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"The ship\'s AI foundation","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/the-ships-ai-foundation"},"nextItem":{"title":"The relativistic sky","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/the-relativistic-sky"}},"content":"The galaxy map now draws from the same star catalogues as the sky, and stars that belong together\\nstay together.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **The map on the catalogue tiers** ([#81](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/81)): 5,687 stars within 25 pc, up from 3,802,\\n  with full-precision positions. \u03b1 Centauri A and B are separate stars you can select.\\n- **Companion stars at their system\'s distance** ([#89](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/89)): a companion within 60\u2033 and\\n  2,000 AU of its primary, agreeing in parallax and proper motion, takes the system\'s distance\\n  rather than its own noisier one. That moved 20,524 companions; Sirius B, for one, now sits with\\n  Sirius A at 8.6 ly.\\n\\n![The galaxy map planning a trip to Sirius A, 8.60 ly](/img/news/map-sirius.jpg)\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nBoth are in the [walkable bridge demo, v0.4.0-dev.1](/news/2026/10/03/walkable-bridge-demo-v0-4-0-dev-1)."},{"id":"/2026/10/03/the-relativistic-sky","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/the-relativistic-sky","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-03-the-relativistic-sky.mdx","source":"@site/news/2026-10-03-the-relativistic-sky.mdx","title":"The relativistic sky","description":"The sky out of the window is now the real one: 335,157 stars over the Milky Way, exposed for a","date":"2026-10-03T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Progress","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/progress","description":"Merged work between releases."},{"inline":false,"label":"Sky","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/sky","description":"The relativistic sky and the star catalogues."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"The relativistic sky","date":"2026-10-03T09:00","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["progress","sky"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"A galaxy map from real catalogues","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/a-galaxy-map-from-real-catalogues"},"nextItem":{"title":"v0.3: plan, commit, transit, arrive","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/02/v0-3-m2-journey"}},"content":"import {ClipFigure} from \'@site/src/components/Clip\';\\n\\nThe sky out of the window is now the real one: 335,157 stars over the Milky Way, exposed for a\\ndark-adapted human eye, with the cosmic background glowing ahead at extreme speeds.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **Starfield v2** ([#67](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/67)): 335,157 stars from CNS5, Gaia GCNS and Hipparcos,\\n  instanced on the GPU, with float64 positions rebased around the ship.\\n- **The Milky Way** behind them: the NOIRLab panorama with the catalogue\'s own stars removed, so\\n  stars are not counted twice, Doppler shifted texel by texel.\\n- **A naked-eye exposure** ([#75](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/75), [#80](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/80)): stars in lux and the sky in\\n  cd/m\xb2, calibrated so the faintest visible star lands at V 6.9 (Crumey\'s model says 6.897). The\\n  HUD always says how it is exposing; the readability aids are off by default and labelled.\\n- **The forward CMB glow** ([#79](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/79), fixed in [#88](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/pull/88)): above \u03b3 \u2248 150 the 2.7 K\\n  microwave background, blueshifted, shows up dead ahead; at \u03b3 707 it is a 3,853.7 K blackbody.\\n\\n<ClipFigure name=\\"cmb\\" caption=\\"\u03b3 20 to 707 through a 20\xb0 lens: the stars crowd into a shrinking ball, then the forward CMB warms from deep red to near white.\\" />\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nM1\'s acceptance step (M1.5b) is still open: the reference renders at five speeds and the 60 fps\\nbench at 1440p with everything on. See the [roadmap](/docs/roadmap)."},{"id":"/2026/10/02/v0-3-m2-journey","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/02/v0-3-m2-journey","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-02-v0-3-m2-journey.md","source":"@site/news/2026-10-02-v0-3-m2-journey.md","title":"v0.3: plan, commit, transit, arrive","description":"The journey core is complete: pick a star, commit, watch both clocks run, and arrive. Once you","date":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"v0.3: plan, commit, transit, arrive","date":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey"],"release_tag":"v0.3.2-m2-journey","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.3.2-m2-journey"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"The relativistic sky","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/03/the-relativistic-sky"},"nextItem":{"title":"v0.2.0: a galaxy map with real numbers","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/01/v0-2-0-m2-map"}},"content":"The journey core is complete: pick a star, commit, watch both clocks run, and arrive. Once you\\ncommit, there is no going back.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **Commit:** hold for 1.5 s. After that the simulation refuses every cancel, and says so.\\n- **Transit and arrival:** the phase, both clocks, the distance flown and the energy radiated,\\n  live, until you arrive.\\n- **Deterministic replay:** a 10,000-tick session replays byte for byte on the AILANG VM and the\\n  interpreter.\\n- v0.3.1 opens straight onto the galaxy map; v0.3.2 adds trackpad zoom and Retina scaling.\\n\\n![Commit, and you cannot take it back](/img/gallery/map-commit.jpg)\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nThe interior of the ship, and a journey you live through on board, are the next milestone (M4).\\n\\n**Releases:** [v0.3.0](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.3.0-m2-journey),\\n[v0.3.1](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.3.1-m2-journey),\\n[v0.3.2](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.3.2-m2-journey) (macOS review builds)"},{"id":"/2026/10/01/v0-2-0-m2-map","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/01/v0-2-0-m2-map","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-10-01-v0-2-0-m2-map.md","source":"@site/news/2026-10-01-v0-2-0-m2-map.md","title":"v0.2.0: a galaxy map with real numbers","description":"The game now opens on a 3D map of the nearby stars. Click one and the simulation plans the trip:","date":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Journey","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/journey","description":"Planning, committing and flying journeys."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"v0.2.0: a galaxy map with real numbers","date":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","journey"],"release_tag":"v0.2.0-m2-map","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.2.0-m2-map"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"v0.3: plan, commit, transit, arrive","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/02/v0-3-m2-journey"},"nextItem":{"title":"v0.1.0: the spike","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/09/27/v0-1-0-m0"}},"content":"The game now opens on a 3D map of the nearby stars. Click one and the simulation plans the trip:\\nyour years against Earth\'s.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- A galaxy map of the nearby-star catalogue: drag to orbit, scroll to zoom, click to plan.\\n- A cruise slider from 0.9c to 0.999999c, spaced evenly in rapidity, 0.99c by default.\\n- Every number on the panel comes straight from the AILANG simulation. \u03b1 Centauri A at 0.99c:\\n  0.6208 years for you, 4.401 for Earth, 1.80 minutes of boost at each end.\\n\\n![The galaxy map planning a trip to \u03b1 Centauri A](/img/gallery/map-plan.jpg)\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nCommitting to the journey and flying it came in the next build.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.2.0-m2-map](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.2.0-m2-map) (macOS review build)"},{"id":"/2026/09/27/v0-1-0-m0","metadata":{"permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/09/27/v0-1-0-m0","editUrl":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/tree/main/website/news/2026-09-27-v0-1-0-m0.md","source":"@site/news/2026-09-27-v0-1-0-m0.md","title":"v0.1.0: the spike","description":"The first review build: an AILANG simulation driving a Godot starfield, with relativity that is","date":"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/release","description":"A versioned GitHub release, with its downloadable build."},{"inline":false,"label":"Sky","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/tags/sky","description":"The relativistic sky and the star catalogues."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Sunholo","title":"Stapledon\'s Voyage team","url":"https://www.sunholo.com","imageURL":"https://ailang.sunholo.com/img/favicon.ico","key":"sunholo","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"v0.1.0: the spike","date":"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z","authors":["sunholo"],"tags":["release","sky"],"release_tag":"v0.1.0-m0","release_url":"https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.1.0-m0"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"v0.2.0: a galaxy map with real numbers","permalink":"/stapledons-godot/news/2026/10/01/v0-2-0-m2-map"}},"content":"The first review build: an AILANG simulation driving a Godot starfield, with relativity that is\\ntested rather than eyeballed.\\n\\n{/* truncate */}\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- The simulation runs in AILANG as a child process, talking one line of JSON per tick with Godot\\n  (about 50 \xb5s per round trip). It flies the ship at 1 g with exact rapidity kinematics.\\n- The starfield: 3,802 nearby stars (CNS5), each aberrated toward the bow, coloured as a\\n  Doppler-shifted blackbody and beamed brighter ahead.\\n- 27 physics reference checks, and 9 cases where the GPU shader must put a star where the CPU\\n  reference says, to under 0.1 px.\\n\\n![The sky at 0, 0.5, 0.9 and 0.99c, looking forward, starboard and astern](/img/news/m0-contact-sheet.jpg)\\n\\n## Not yet\\n\\nNo Milky Way behind the stars, one axis of motion, and star colours from the spectral class\\nonly. All three were fixed in M1.\\n\\n**Release:** [v0.1.0-m0](https://github.com/sunholo-data/stapledons-godot/releases/tag/v0.1.0-m0) (macOS review build)"}]}}')}}]);